# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The data contract (see README.md § Data)
#
# Default is still "data doesn't belong in git", but a repo whose every notebook
# dies on cell 1 with FileNotFoundError can't be read, reviewed or assessed. So
# the rule is now: track whatever is small enough to ship AND is needed to run
# the main-line notebooks; ignore the bulk that is regenerable.
#
# Tracked (~22 MB total):
#   data/raw/*.jsonl                    the 6 labelled exports — source of truth,
#                                       12.5 MB compressed, makes 01 runnable
#   data/raw/*.usecase.json             the per-corpus briefs (a few KB each)
#   data/processed/papers_combined.parquet   9.3 MB, cleaned corpus + embedding col
#   data/processed/papers_fe_slim.parquet    0.3 MB, the FE table minus emb_* blocks
#
# Ignored (regenerable, ~600 MB):
#   papers_fe.parquet (106 MB)          rebuild: notebooks/04_feature_engineering
#   papers_fe_synergy*.parquet (173 MB) external-validation artifacts
#   embeddings_cache/ (295 MB)          paid API / Modal GPU output
#   data/benchsets_v1/ (92 MB)          not ours to ship — 28 externally-published
#                                       screening collections (SYNERGY CC0, Nykvist
#                                       CC BY, Mendeley CC BY). Re-downloadable from
#                                       the sources its own README lists, so it's
#                                       bulk-and-regenerable like the rest of this
#                                       block, not a 5th tracked file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/benchsets_v1
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/processed/README.md
!data/raw/*.jsonl
!data/raw/*.usecase.json
!data/processed/papers_combined.parquet
!data/processed/papers_fe_slim.parquet

# Local fastembed model cache, if pointed here
.cache/

.ipynb_checkpoints/

# CatBoost's own per-fit training-log directory, written wherever a fit runs locally
catboost_info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# reports/ is now an OUTPUT DIRECTORY ONLY.
#
# The 57 written-up reports that used to live here were removed to slim the repo (see
# README § "Removed reports"; they are recoverable from git history at 75c14de). What
# remains is a directory that notebooks and scripts write into: `02_eda_quickstart` and
# `03_eda_full` save their figures here, and ~76 scripts write .md/.csv/.json outputs.
#
# So everything in here is ignored and only `.gitkeep` is tracked. That .gitkeep is
# load-bearing, not decoration: notebook 02 does `REPORTS_DIR = Path("../../reports")`
# with no mkdir, so without a tracked file holding the directory open, a fresh clone
# would fail when the notebook tries to save.
#
# To commit a write-up again, force-add it: `git add -f reports/<file>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# Node dependencies for scripts/md2docx.js (the whitepaper -> .docx renderer). The project
# itself is Python; this is document tooling only. `npm install` restores it from
# package-lock.json.
node_modules/
